The goal of this project is to create a repository of Forest Growth and Yield Models in Canada.
I would like the project to reside on Github.
I would like for collaborators to be able to add information pertaining to their GY models or models that they are aware of and which are "in use".
I would like for this project to be private at first, but the intention is to have a public version.
I would like for the project to allow users to perform queries based characteristics of the GY models.
I would like to also have an interactive map which displays Canada (simple) and area (defined by Provincial Boundaries) where each GY model is applicable.

The folder that holds the project is located here: C:\CanGrowthModels

To start, i have two CSVs which are currently minimally populated: models_schema_definition.csv and models_template.csv
I also have R scripts that would serve to validate the information about the models (e.g., flag errors in species names and provide corrections)
I also have pdf and word files. Do not look at these unless i give permission. I will convert them to markdown files and ask an ai agent to scan them. 
